{
  peppy_schema: "contract/v1",
  manifest: {
    name: "sensor_mounts",
    tag: "v1",
    description: [
      "Where a robot carries its sensors: the robot frame, and for each of its sensors, such as a camera, a lidar or a range sensor, the contract it streams on, the sensor's frame in the robot's tree, and the part that carries it.",
      "camera_geometry gives a camera's own geometry and says that where the camera sits on the robot is not the camera's to know; this contract names the camera's frame in the robot's tree, and transforms places it. lidar_2d, lidar_3d and range_sensor say the same of where their sensor sits. A consumer places a measurement in the robot frame, which describe_sensors names, or in any other frame of the robot, by a lookup of the sensor's frame in transforms at the time of the measurement as the sensor's contract gives it: a reading's timestamp; for a lidar_2d scan, the sensor frame's places at its first and its last ray, between which each ray's place is interpolated by its share of the sweep, as laser_geometry's transformLaserScanToPointCloud places a scan's rays; and for a lidar_3d cloud, the sensor frame's place at the cloud's timestamp, for each of its points, as pointcloud_to_laserscan transforms a cloud. transform_lookup answers such a lookup for a node that holds no tree.",
      "Sensor frame. The frame that the sensor's contract defines, which sensor_kinds names: for a camera the colour optical frame as camera_geometry defines it, and for a lidar or a range sensor the sensor frame as lidar_2d, lidar_3d or range_sensor defines it. It is a link of the robot's URDF, on a fixed joint to the link of the part that carries the sensor.",
      "The implementer is robot_identity's, and answers from the robot's model, for as long as it runs.",
      "No member has a mark.",
    ],
  },
  interfaces: {
    services: [
      {
        name: "describe_sensors",
        description: "Give the robot frame, and every sensor the robot's design carries, such as a camera, a lidar or a range sensor: its name, the contract it streams on, its frame and the part that carries it. A sensor of the design that no node streams is listed too, under the name its node runs under once one streams it. A robot without sensors answers with empty arrays.",
        response_message_format: {
          robot_frame: { $type: "string", $description: "The robot frame of transforms: the root link of the robot's URDF." },
          sensor_names: { $type: "array", $items: "string", $description: "The names the robot's sensors run under (chest, wrist_left, lidar), in the robot's fixed order. sensor_kinds, sensor_frames and carried_by are index-aligned with this array." },
          sensor_kinds: { $type: "array", $items: "string", $description: "The contract each sensor streams on, which defines its frame, such as \"rgb_camera\", \"rgbd_camera\", \"lidar_2d\", \"lidar_3d\" or \"range_sensor\", in sensor_names order." },
          sensor_frames: { $type: "array", $items: "string", $description: "The frame of each sensor in transforms, a link of the robot's URDF, in sensor_names order." },
          carried_by: { $type: "array", $items: "string", $description: "The part that carries each sensor, by the name its contract addresses it under, such as an arm's name, or \"\" for a sensor fixed to the base, in sensor_names order." },
        },
      },
    ],
  },
}
